{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794984658,"nonce":"a05+EYWcrc4yCHjN/mZna557yXs=","title":"Plan a managed assets database/service layered on the open-source hxn-file/hxn-assets monorepo. The same SDK/catalog/projection contracts must serve local apps, open-source self-hosting and a hosted offering. hxnme will consume those contracts later; users do not need the managed service for local asset loading, saves or preferences.","message":"Proposed hosted roles: object storage (Cloudflare R2 initially, with an S3-compatible adapter contract) stores immutable bytes/cooked variants; cloud KyuGraph stores asset/catalog metadata, provenance and opted-in entity/world relationships; Cloudflare Workers expose authenticated HTTP APIs; Durable Objects coordinate tenant/catalog revisions, upload state, idempotency and live subscriptions. KyuGraph runs as its own cloud service, not assumed to fit in the Workers/DO runtime. Investigate its existing cloud page store and Arrow Flight/API surface before choosing a gateway.\n\nClient boundary: AssetSource/CatalogSource/ProjectionSink contracts return hxn.Future values. Auth is application-supplied; never embed a service secret in a game or browser build. Remote descriptors carry version/revision, content ID, byte length/media type and expiring read authorization. Local/catalog/blob caches operate independently of cloud availability. Catalog/world identity and immutable content identity remain distinct.\n\nTenant isolation: namespaces on catalogs, content keys, graph partitions and entity/world IDs; scoped capabilities/signed uploads/downloads; authorization at every object and relationship query. Private content is not globally presence-queryable or cross-tenant deduplicated by default. Opt-in public sharing is explicit. Graph projections include only annotated/application-selected data, not saves or preferences by default.\n\nPublication protocol: reserve an idempotent upload; stream bytes to a staged/multipart object; verify server-side length/digest; publish an immutable object; commit a new catalog revision and durable projection/outbox event through the tenant coordinator; apply/replay KyuGraph projection updates. Do not claim one distributed transaction across R2, DO and KyuGraph. Readers use published revision manifests; pending uploads/failed graph sync remain explicit. Test interruption at each transition, duplicates, replay, conflicting revisions and read-after-publish. Retain/reconcile orphan objects and delete only after reference/retention checks.\n\nWorld-space projection: versioned entity-instance updates include tenant, world/coordinate-space ID, entity ID, transform/bounds and revision. Batch/coalesce high-frequency motion; graph queries never run in the render path. Separate authoritative game/scene state from rebuildable catalog/spatial graph projections. Support lookups combining content/asset relationships, entity hierarchy and region/bounds constraints; validate actual KyuGraph spatial indexing capabilities before promising them.\n\nHosted product layer: managed tenant provisioning, quotas/metering, upload/download policies, backups, retention, synchronization/live events, observability and operational support. Keep provider-specific coordination and object-store code separate from the portable SDK and self-hostable contracts. Open-source users can deploy compatible infrastructure and configure their own endpoints.\n\nPrerequisites/acceptance: finish M0 platform I/O and persistent save/pref round trips; make source/catalog APIs backend-neutral; deterministic content IDs/variant manifests and opt-in annotations; local/self-hosted/hosted adapter conformance; tenant/capability tests; bounded requests and upload sizes; network reconnect/offline reads; failed upload/publish/graph replay; large object streaming; region/world relationship queries; documented consistency and deletion semantics.\n\nRelated file-access issue 49624d318b0b2d8efec7e26ccd271c6004e5150e4fe8b5dd33e105ee21c472fb and opt-in projection plan af5e85a; parent hxnme plan 88ad5eff5f418581d790175f13ad89d85d24c50e980dca23033b4d884329b3cd. This is planning for the hosted layer; it does not make a service dependency mandatory in the M0 library.","files":null}]}